WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.960
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.630
Your name is Rita?

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.350
Rita, where are you from originally?

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.683
- [Rita] Tucson, Arizona.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.670
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your childhood.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:22.930
You grow up with both of your parents?

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:26.290
- No, I just grew up with
my mama and she drink a lot,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.370
havin' parties and I didn't
want to be with nobody

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.810
but my momma.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.963
And when her died, I had
to live in a hospital.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.460
- [Interviewer] When
did your mom pass away?

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.640
- When I was 12 years old

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.390
and I wanted to die with
her, but I couldn't.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.003
They put me in the hospital.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.430
But I tried to get in the casket with her

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.660
and they put me to sleep.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.713
When I woke up, I was in the hospital.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.630
They shoot me with some stuff

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.230
and now I gotta take it all my life.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.433
It's Thorazine.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.013
- [Interviewer] So, what'd you say,

00:01:04.013 --> 00:01:04.880
you tried to get in the casket?

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:05.713
- Yeah.

00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:06.546
- [Interviewer] With your mom?

00:01:06.546 --> 00:01:07.640
- Yeah and I wouldn't let her go,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.460
but they put me to sleep

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.123
and when I woke up, I was in a hospital.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.720
It's called Palo Verde Hospital.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.993
Palo Verde Street, Tucson, Arizona.

00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:26.210
- [Interviewer] So, your
mom passes away at 12

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.600
and you went where?

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.530
- I went to Palo Verde
Hospital in Tucson, Arizona

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.891
and then I lived at the county hospital

00:01:34.891 --> 00:01:39.240
at Tucson Medical Center

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.840
in the mental hospital in--

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.150
- [Interviewer] Oh, you
went to a mental hospital?

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.480
- Yeah, I lived in the ,like the exodus

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.480
and (mumbles) I don't know the other name.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.463
I wasn't able to take care
of myself until I was 52.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:03.223
I'm 57, I just turned 57 January the 13th,

00:02:04.452 --> 00:02:07.010
and they say I'mma die
at the county hospital

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:08.210
in three to six weeks,

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.953
'cause they found some
black stuff in my brain.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.503
- [Interviewer] Sorry can you repeat that?

00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:15.336
I'm sorry.

00:02:15.336 --> 00:02:17.770
- They found some black spots in my brain

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.520
at the county hospital on Morengo street.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.353
- [Interviewer] And what'd they tell you?

00:02:21.353 --> 00:02:24.010
- And they said I'mma die
from three to six weeks,

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.270
they couldn't save me but
they couldn't help me until--

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.970
- [Interviewer] So it
sounds like brain cancer?

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:28.803
- Yeah.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.850
- [Interviewer] You were in a
mental hospital for how long--

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:34.683
how much of your life?

00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:37.510
- At the exodus until 2014.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:42.440
- [Interviewer] So you've
been in the hospital

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.273
for most of your life.

00:02:43.273 --> 00:02:45.003
- [Rita] Yeah until now.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.770
They let me be on my own, but I gotta do--

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.180
get nurse and stuff
check on me all the time

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.180
right there by the forts.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:02.667
The nurse comes, I gotta go see 'em

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:06.517
and they check on me and they
put a machine on my head.

00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:09.942
- [Interviewer] Where
do you live right now?

00:03:09.942 --> 00:03:12.053
- I just walk around.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:14.800
- [Interviewer] You're
just out in the street?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:15.633
- Yeah.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.067
- [Interviewer] Do you have any family?

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.560
Do you have any kids?
- [Rita] No, only me.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.050
I'm here.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.160
- [Interviewer] You spent your
whole life in the hospital,

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.210
so it's hard to have a family, right?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.990
- [Rita] Yeah, I only know my sister,

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.820
but I don't know her.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.080
I know I got a sister, but
I only stay with my momma.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.050
My mother used to take
my sisters to her sis--

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.853
My auntie's house, and keep me with her.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.920
- [Interviewer] And do you mess around

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.490
with any of the drugs
that are on the street?

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:55.290
- [Rita] Yes, when I was
prostituting I did drugs.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:04:00.290
And then I had sex and I caught germs.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.100
- [Interviewer] So you
started prostituting

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.290
when you came out of the hospital?

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.123
- [Rita] Yeah.

00:04:05.123 --> 00:04:08.230
- [Interviewer] At 54,
something like that?

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.883
- No, (mumbles) yeah.

00:04:15.445 --> 00:04:16.620
- [Interviewer] And now you just found out

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.790
you have brain cancer?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:22.790
- Yeah I found out in
2018 that I had aneurysm,

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.283
I can't say it.

00:04:28.285 --> 00:04:30.560
- [Interviewer] And what
do you do for money?

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.393
How do you survive?

00:04:31.393 --> 00:04:33.860
- I sit on the ground sometimes

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:37.020
and tell 'em they could
give me food or help

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.220
or donations, so I eat leftovers.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.053
- [Interviewer] And
then sometimes you work

00:04:41.053 --> 00:04:42.620
as a prostitute as well?

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.453
Yeah.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.260
- [Interviewer] What's your view of life?

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.890
I mean, do you think life is just cruel?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.000
- No, it's what we make of it,

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.090
but it's cruel to me
because I don't know nobody

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:00.410
I don't have no family.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.820
- [Interviewer] Do you have any friends?

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.110
- No 'cause, I don't have friends

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.720
because I feel like I'm different.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.230
Sometimes they say I'm
retarded or something.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.410
I just wanna be by myself.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.700
- [Interviewer] Have you ever had friends?

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.040
- [Rita] Yeah.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:17.873
- [Interviewer] In the hospital?

00:05:17.873 --> 00:05:20.410
- My momma's friends, I
had my momma's friends.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.323
- [Interviewer] Oh okay.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:25.670
Well Rita thank you so much

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.110
for sharing you story.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.011
It's a tragedy.

00:05:28.011 --> 00:05:30.140
- It's not a story, it's for real.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.693
- [Interviewer] I know it's real.

